{"case_id": "v4.case.corrected-b01-01", "displayed_text": "Alderbridge makes several wellbeing services available to every employee: an Employee Assistance Programme (EAP) offering confidential, externally provided telephone counselling and self‑help resources that anyone may access directly and free of charge at any time; access to a named mental health first aider at each site for an initial, non‑clinical supportive conversation and signposting; manager‑initiated wellbeing referrals to occupational health (with employee consent except where urgent safeguarding requires escalation); proactive additional debrief opportunities after a death; signposting to independent financial guidance via the EAP; and consideration of reasonable adjustments where a health condition affects someone’s ability to work.\n\nYour induction and onboarding process explicitly embeds checks and routes to these supports: the mandatory induction buddy is introduced to the new starter on day one and serves as an informal, approachable point of contact with a formal check‑in partway through the mandatory four‑week buddy period (and extension if both agree); the New Starter Onboarding Checklist requires the induction handbook to be issued on day one and must be completed and returned to HR within two weeks; and the buddy/induction guidance and onboarding checklist are stated to work alongside the Staff Supervision and Appraisal arrangements, so the buddy introduction, the day‑one handbook issuance and the scheduled follow‑ups form the documented steps by which the induction checks you know how to access support.", "finished_at": "2026-11-12T10:56:50+00:00", "frozen_scope": "primary", "needs_opt_in": ["5323cd6b-8b7a-40f9-98b0-9413c75f643e"], "needs_pipeline_exercised": true, "observation": {"assistant_message_kind": "grounded_answer", "case_id": "v4.case.corrected-b01-01", "contextualisation": {"clarification_question": null, "contextualiser_version": "authorised-user-turns-needs-v1", "interpretat